# UI Redesign: Quiet Editorial Design System

Migrate the Nudge app's entire frontend from the current dark-mode, CSS Modules design to the "Quiet Editorial" editorial light-mode aesthetic as designed in the Stitch mockups.

## Overview of the New Design

- **Theme**: Warm off-white "paper" background (`#fdf8f5`), Terracotta primary (`#99462a`), charcoal ink text
- **Typography**: Newsreader (serif) for content/headlines + Inter (sans) for UI chrome/labels
- **Layout**: Left sidebar navigation on desktop (replaces top tab bar), bottom nav on mobile
- **Style**: Flat, no shadows. Tonal layering. Quiet and editorial.
- **Icons**: Google Material Symbols Outlined

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Tailwind CSS**: The Stitch mockups are built with Tailwind CSS v3 + the Quiet Editorial custom theme. This is a significant departure from the current Vanilla CSS + CSS Modules approach. Since this is purely a UI layer change with no backend impact, this is the recommended approach — but confirm before proceeding.

> [!WARNING]
> **Dark mode is removed**: The new design is light-mode only. The current dark theme (`#0d0d0f` background) will be completely replaced. There is no dark mode toggle in the Stitch designs.

> [!NOTE]
> **App shell change**: Navigation moves from a **horizontal top tab bar** to a **vertical left sidebar** (desktop) + **bottom bar** (mobile). This requires a structural rewrite of `App.jsx` and `App.module.css`.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1: Foundation — Design System & App Shell

#### [MODIFY] `src/styles/global.css`
- Remove all existing dark-mode tokens.
- Add Google Fonts import: `Newsreader` + `Inter` + `Material Symbols Outlined`.
- Define the full Quiet Editorial CSS variable set from `DESIGN.md`.
- Add base body styles: `background: #fdf8f5`, `color: #1c1b19`, `font-family: Newsreader`.

#### [NEW] Install Tailwind CSS v3
- Add via CDN in `index.html` (same pattern as mockups) OR install as npm dependency and configure `tailwind.config.js`.
- Recommended: npm install for production builds. CDN for quick iteration.
- Configure the custom theme tokens (colors, spacing, fontFamily, fontSize, borderRadius) from the Stitch config.

#### [MODIFY] `src/App.jsx` — New App Shell
- Replace the horizontal `<nav>` tab bar with:
  - **Desktop**: `<aside>` left sidebar (264px wide, `border-r border-outline-variant`) with vertical nav links + `border-l-2 border-primary` active indicator.
  - **Mobile**: Fixed `<nav>` bottom bar with icon + label pairs.
- Logo "Nudge" renders in Newsreader, Terracotta color.
- Active tab: Terracotta text, bold, left border highlight, `bg-surface-container-low` background.
- Keep all existing `activeTab`, `distractionCount`, provider wrapping — just change the chrome.

#### [MODIFY] `src/App.module.css`
- Rewrite to support the new sidebar layout (`flex-row` shell, fixed sidebar, scrollable main).
- Or remove entirely and use Tailwind utility classes directly in JSX.

---

### Phase 2: Timer Tab — `CurrentTask.jsx`

**Reference**: `timer_dashboard_desktop_web/screen.png` + `code.html`

**New layout** (split two-column on desktop):
- **Left column**: Circular timer ring — warm off-white circle with `border-outline` 1px border. No gradient/glow. Large `48px` Newsreader numeral in center. Start/Reset buttons below (Terracotta primary + ghost).
- **Right column**: 
  - "CURRENT FOCUS" label (Inter 11px, all caps, tracked) + task title in `headline-xl` Newsreader.
  - Elapsed time with `schedule` material icon.
  - Thin `16px` horizontal divider.
  - "COMING UP NEXT" section — list of pending tasks with empty checkbox squares.
- **No task active**: Show same layout but with "No active task" placeholder copy.

**Files to modify**:
- `src/components/CurrentTask/CurrentTask.jsx` — full JSX rewrite
- `src/components/CurrentTask/CurrentTask.module.css` — full CSS rewrite (or migrate to Tailwind)

---

### Phase 3: Tasks Tab — `TaskList.jsx`

**Reference**: `tasks_desktop_web/screen.png` + `code.html`

**New layout**:
- Page header: "Tasks" (`headline-xl` Newsreader) + "Today's Focus" subtext.
- Add Task input: `bg-surface-container-low` pill with `add` material icon on left. No border at rest, `outline-variant` border on focus.
- Task list: borderless rows separated by 1px `border-surface-variant` dividers. Generous `24px` vertical padding.
  - Custom checkbox: 20×20px, `border-outline`, Terracotta fill with white checkmark when checked.
  - Task title: `body-md` Newsreader.
  - Est. time chip: `surface-variant` background, pill-shaped, `label-sm` Inter.
  - Edit/delete icons: appear on hover (`opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100`).
  - Completed tasks: `line-through`, `text-on-surface-variant`.
- Active task at top with left terracotta indicator strip.

**Files to modify**:
- `src/components/Tasks/TaskList.jsx` — JSX rewrite
- `src/components/Tasks/TaskList.module.css` — CSS rewrite / migrate to Tailwind

---

### Phase 4: Summary Tab — `Summary.jsx`

**Reference**: `summary_desktop_web/screen.png` + `code.html`

**New layout** (editorial document style, max-width 720px centered):
- Page header: "Daily Summary" (`headline-xl`) + date (`body-md`, muted).
- **AI Insight card**: `bg-surface-container-low`, 1px `outline-variant` border, rounded-lg. `auto_awesome` icon + "AI Insight" label in Terracotta. Body text in Newsreader.
- **Deep Work Time**: Large `headline-xl` metric.
- **Top Distractions**: Header + list rows with time chips (same pill style as tasks).
- **What You Worked On**: Article cards with project name, time chip, and descriptive Newsreader body paragraph.
- **Actions section**: "Generate Now" Terracotta button + "Export to Markdown" ghost link (underlined on hover).
- Error banner: keep inline error banner logic from current implementation.

**Files to modify**:
- `src/components/Summary/Summary.jsx` — JSX rewrite
- `src/components/Summary/Summary.module.css` — CSS rewrite

---

### Phase 5: Settings Tab — `Settings.jsx`

**Reference**: `settings_desktop_web/screen.png` + `code.html`

**New layout** (document-style, max-width 720px):
- Page header: "Settings" (`headline-xl`) + subtitle text.
- **AI Configuration section**: `headline-lg` section title + body description. AI model selector + Gemini key input (`bg-surface-container-low`, `border-outline-variant`, Terracotta focus ring).
- **System section**: Launch on startup toggle — custom Tailwind peer-checked toggle (Terracotta fill when on).
- **Work Hours section**: 2-column time inputs grid.
- `<hr>` dividers (`border-outline-variant/50`) between sections.
- "Save Preferences" button: Terracotta, right-aligned, `rounded-DEFAULT`.

**Files to modify**:
- `src/components/Settings/Settings.jsx` — JSX rewrite
- `src/components/Settings/Settings.module.css` — CSS rewrite

---

### Phase 6: Cleanup

- Remove old dark-mode-specific CSS variables from `global.css`.
- Remove unused `--color-danger`, `--bg-base`, etc. aliases (replace with Tailwind).
- Verify `SummaryContext`, `TimerContext`, `ActiveTaskContext` are untouched (logic only, no UI).
- Verify all backend API calls remain unchanged.

---

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification (in running `npm run tauri dev`)
1. App shell: sidebar renders at desktop, bottom bar on mobile (resize window to test).
2. Timer tab: circular ring shows, active task shows right-column content, no task shows placeholder.
3. Tasks tab: add task input works, checkbox checks/unchecks correctly, hover reveals edit/delete.
4. Summary tab: "Generate Now" fires API, AI insight card renders with Newsreader body text, export downloads `.md`.
5. Settings tab: toggles, inputs, and save button all wire up to backend correctly.
6. Navigation: switching tabs via sidebar + bottom bar both work, active state highlights correctly.

### Key Design Rules to Verify
- No dark backgrounds anywhere.
- Terracotta (`#99462a`) used only for: active nav, primary buttons, focus rings.
- Newsreader for all headlines and body content.
- Inter for all labels, buttons, chips.
- No box shadows except where explicitly permitted (modal/floating elements only).
